{
  "name": "Manage Google Calendar and Google Tasks from Telegram text or voice notes with a Gemini agent",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Manage Google Calendar and Google Tasks from Telegram text or voice notes with a Gemini agent\n\nTalk to your calendar. Send your Telegram bot a message or a voice note like \"What's on tomorrow?\", \"Lunch with Priya Friday 1pm\" or \"Remind me to renew my passport by the 30th\", and a Gemini agent reads and updates Google Calendar and Google Tasks for you, then replies in plain language. Only the Telegram users you allow can use it.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Receive Telegram message** gets each message; **Is this an allowed user?** drops anyone not in your `allowed_user_ids`.\n2. Voice notes are downloaded and transcribed by Gemini; text messages are used as they are.\n3. **Calendar and tasks assistant** (AI Agent) knows today's date in your timezone and can get and create calendar events, list open tasks, add tasks with due dates and complete tasks.\n4. **Remember the conversation** keeps the last 10 messages per chat, so follow-ups like \"move it to 3pm\" work in context.\n5. **Format reply** strips markdown, shows what it heard for voice notes and splits long replies.\n\n### Setup\n1. Create a bot with @BotFather and add a **Telegram** credential.\n2. Add **Google Gemini (PaLM) API** (free key at aistudio.google.com), **Google Calendar** and **Google Tasks** OAuth credentials.\n3. In **Set assistant settings** put your Telegram user ID (message @userinfobot) and timezone.\n4. Activate the workflow and say hi to your bot.\n\n### Customization\n- Change `calendar` in the calendar tools from `primary` to another calendar ID.\n- Add more tools to the agent, such as Gmail or Google Sheets.\n\nFailure alerts: fill in the alert node in **Alert on errors** and choose this workflow under **Settings > Error workflow**.",
        "height": 960,
        "width": 600
      },
